# Crystal Barricade: "You have hexproof" (CR 702.11c) - its controller can't be the target of spells or abilities their
# opponents control, but can be the target of their own. Bot1 casts Crystal Barricade on turn 1 and then its own Lightning
# Bolt at itself (the positive control: hexproof stops only opponents, Bot1 goes to 17). On turn 2 Bot2's Lightning Bolt
# can't target Bot1 (refusal, with the red mana to cast it), though it can target Crystal Barricade. "Other creatures you
# control" leaves Crystal Barricade out (CR 615.1): the Bolt's 3 damage stays marked on it and nothing is prevented.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Crystal Barricade
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Crystal Barricade.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Crystal Barricade)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Crystal Barricade.Damage = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Prevented = (absent)
